{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ויקחהו", :translit "vayikacheihu", :gloss "and he took him"} {:he "ויקח מאתם את שמעון", :translit "vayikach me'item et shim'on", :gloss "and he took from them Shimon"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling without vav in ויקחהו signals only one brother acted"}], :frame {:text "The verse says 'they took him and cast him into the pit,' yet the defective spelling of ויקחהו (missing the second vav) narrows the plural action to a single individual. Genesis 42:24 records that Joseph 'took Shimon from among them,' identifying Shimon as the specific brother who seized Joseph. Ba'al HaTurim links the defective spelling to this later verse to identify the sole actor.", :sources ["Genesis 37:24" "Genesis 42:24"]}} {:quotes [{:he "רק", :translit "rak", :gloss "only / empty"} {:he "כי לא דבר רק הוא", :translit "ki lo davar rak hu", :gloss "for it is not an empty thing"} {:he "מים אין בו אבל יש בו נחשים ועקרבים", :translit "mayim ein bo aval yesh bo nachashim va'akravim", :gloss "water it did not have but it had snakes and scorpions"} {:he "נחש שרף ועקרב וצמאון אשר אין מים", :translit "nachash saraf va'akrav vitzama'on asher ein mayim", :gloss "snake serpent and scorpion and thirst where there is no water"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["רק" "כי לא דבר רק הוא"]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: the word רק links the pit in Genesis to the verse in Deuteronomy to derive that the pit contained snakes and scorpions"}], :frame {:text "The phrase 'והבור רק אין בו מים' is read by the Tanna devei Eliyahu as 'the pit was empty only of water,' meaning it still contained snakes and scorpions. This interpretation appears in Shabbat 22a in the sugya discussing the miracle of the jug of oil on Hanukkah, where the Gemara deduces from the word רק that the pit held snakes and scorpions. Deuteronomy 8:15, which lists 'נחש שרף ועקרב' alongside thirst in a place with no water, serves as the source text for what else a waterless pit contains.", :sources ["Shabbat 22a" "Deuteronomy 8:15"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Defective spelling without vav in ויקחהו signals only one brother acted", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["רק" "כי לא דבר רק הוא"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "רק", :refs ["Genesis 6:5" "Genesis 14:24" "Genesis 19:8" "Genesis 20:11" "Genesis 24:8" "Genesis 26:29" "Genesis 37:24" "Genesis 41:40"], :n 107, :lens :exact} {:phrase "כי לא דבר רק הוא", :refs ["Deuteronomy 32:47"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Gezeirah shavah: the word רק links the pit in Genesis to the verse in Deuteronomy to derive that the pit contained snakes and scorpions", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:10:35.883540030Z", :model "glm-5.2"}